/P 172 0 R
/E (Every August, Ashenda marks the end of Filseta, a two-week fasting period honoring the Virgin Mary in the Ethiopian Orthodox Tewahedo Church. Thousands of girls in Northern Ethiopia dress in white cotton embroidered dresses and wear skirts made of tall green grass \(called ashenda\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
